{"name":"Mirage","hex":"#373f43","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mirage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An optical phenomenon in which light is refracted through a layer of hot air close to the ground, often giving the illusion of a body of water.","An illusion."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause to appear as or like a mirage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mirage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mirage","blocks":[{"text":"A mirage is a naturally occurring optical phenomenon in which light rays bend via refraction to produce a displaced image of distant objects or the sky. The word comes to English via the French (se) mirer, from the Latin mirari, meaning \"to look at, to wonder at\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Farallon_Islands_at_inferior_mirage_no_mirage_and_superior_mirage.jpg/330px-Farallon_Islands_at_inferior_mirage_no_mirage_and_superior_mirage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirage","wikidata":"Q308762"},{"title":"Mirage (Fleetwood Mac album)","blocks":[{"text":"Mirage is the thirteenth studio album by the British and American rock band Fleetwood Mac, released on 2 July 1982 by Warner Bros. Records. This studio effort's soft rock sound stood in stark contrast to its more experimental predecessor, 1979's Tusk. Mirage yielded several singles: \"Hold Me\", \"Gypsy\", \"Love in Store\", \"Oh Diane\", and \"Can't Go Back\". In addition, \"Wish You Were Here\" was released in Jamaica only, and topped the Jamaican singles chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/76/Fleetwood_Mac_-_Mirage.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirage_(Fleetwood_Mac_album)","wikidata":"Q594244"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Desertmirage.jpg/250px-Desertmirage.j